cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AFF3CT in your research, please cite the SoftwareX article
  below (preferred citation).
title: "AFF3CT: A Fast Forward Error Correction Toolbox!"
type: software
version: 4.7.1
date-released: 2026-09-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aff3ct/aff3ct"
url: "https://aff3ct.github.io"
abstract: >-
  AFF3CT is an open source toolbox dedicated to Forward Error Correction
  (FEC or channel coding). It supports a broad range of codes, from turbo
  codes and Low-Density Parity-Check (LDPC) codes to polar codes. Written in
  C++, it can be used as a simulator to evaluate algorithm characteristics, or
  as a library in Software Defined Radio (SDR) systems. Most decoder
  implementations target low latency and high throughput (multiple Gb/s on
  modern CPUs) through multi-threading and SIMD vectorization.
keywords:
  - forward error correction
  - channel coding
  - LDPC codes
  - polar codes
  - turbo codes
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - software defined radio
  - SIMD
  - C++
